# Environments / secrets
.env
.env.*
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*

# Build output
bin/
obj/
plugin/bin/
plugin/obj/
installer/bin/
installer/obj/
thunderstore/build/
dist/
# Mastered music pack OGGs + cover ship via the music-ar* release assets, never
# through git (a re-master would otherwise become permanent repo history).
# Masters remain local-only.
plugin/music/
# Thunderstore template mirror of the same files (pack step copies them in at pack
# time; the template dir is otherwise git-tracked, so ignore the music subtree BY NAME
# or every re-master enters public history).
thunderstore/SidsCompetitiveRounds_upload/plugins/music/

# Log captures and one-off drops
logs-snapshot/
*.log
# ...except the committed test evidence. Each report under this directory names
# the stdout it was assembled from, in a `stdout:` header, and is rebuilt from
# those bytes by assemble-evidence.py. A report naming a log the repository does
# not carry is exactly the defect that rule exists to stop: a number nobody on a
# fresh clone can re-derive (#302). These captures are produced by the committed
# instruments beside them, print repository-relative paths only, and carry no
# connection string.
#
# PER PRODUCER, NOT `*.log`. The negation used to re-include every `.log` that
# landed in this directory, produced or not, which is a rule that cannot refuse
# anything (#342): a file nothing in this tree writes was admitted by the same
# line as a capture, and an `add -A` over a working directory would carry it.
# Each pattern below is the capture of ONE committed instrument beside it, and
# the instrument prints that name in its own stdout header, so the set is
# derivable rather than remembered.
# test_the_evidence_log_negation_admits_only_produced_logs compares the two
# sets in BOTH directions: a pattern no instrument produces reds, and a capture
# an instrument names that no pattern admits reds.
!backend/tests/evidence/*-suite-run.log
!backend/tests/evidence/*-pg-controls.log
!backend/tests/evidence/*-mutation-run.log
!backend/tests/evidence/*-citation-pin.log
!backend/tests/evidence/*-freeze-guard.log
!backend/tests/evidence/*-repin-run.log
!backend/tests/evidence/*-suites-assembly-run.log
!backend/tests/evidence/*-residual-reach.log

# Tool caches
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.user
*.userprefs

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
# Office lock files (created while an .xlsx/.docx is open)
~$*

# Internal docs — KEEP LOCAL ONLY. These contain IPs, server paths, infra
# details, handoff notes, and task priorities that should never land in a
# public commit. History was scrubbed in the v1.20.0 post-release pass;
# assume anything previously published remains cached on forks/clones.
CLAUDE.md
SETUP.md
.claude/
docs/HANDOFF.md
docs/TODO.md
docs/learnings.md
# The writer replaces that file through a temp copy beside it. If the replace
# fails (on Windows, any process holding the file open is enough), the temp is
# a complete copy of the same local-only content, and the ignore above matches
# one exact name.
docs/learnings.md.*
docs/deploy-reference.md
docs/SECURITY_ACTION_ITEMS.md
docs/https-migration.md
docs/bug140-session-analysis.md
docs/ffa-configurable-lobbies.md
docs/localization-design.md
docs/spectator-design.md
scripts/

# Dual-AI (Codex CLI) setup — LOCAL ONLY, same reason as the internal docs
# above. AGENTS.md mirrors CLAUDE.md's operational context for Codex; the
# collab scratch + dual-AI guides reference infra/workflow. The docs/ ignores
# are per-FILE (not per-dir), so each new doc is listed explicitly.
AGENTS.md
AGENTS.override.md
.codex/
ai-collab/
docs/DUAL-AI-SETUP.md
docs/CODEX-CHEATSHEET.md
scr-tour-script.md

# NuGet
packages/
*.nupkg

# Python caches (defensive — the backend runs in Docker, no local venv expected)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Thunderstore release zip artifacts — attach to GH release, don't track in git
thunderstore/*.zip
_cm.txt

# Local analysis scratch (review-agent caches) — never publish
*.pkl

# Player Cards renderer fonts: fetched by backend/api/assets/fonts/fetch_fonts.py, pinned by fonts.lock.json
backend/api/assets/fonts/*.ttf
backend/api/assets/fonts/*.otf
backend/api/assets/fonts/*.ttc
backend/api/assets/fonts/*.part
backend/tests/_out/
# Working scratch left in the repo root by tooling; never content.
scratchpad/
